, and prediction markets near 95 percent for Republicans all point to a comfortable GOP hold despite the open seat. The lone late poll showing a closer race is a partisan-sponsored outlier against overwhelming structural evidence.", "watch": "A late independent poll showing Gronli within single digits, or a major Jackley scandal, would be the main signal of a genuine race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Open seat: Dusty Johnson (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "South Dakota's at-large House seat is open after Dusty Johnson retired to run for governor, but the district's Republican fundamentals remain strong. Former attorney general Marty Jackley won the GOP primary and enters the general election with a large financial advantage, over $1 million on hand, while Democrat Nikki Gronli has raised a fraction of that and has no outside support on record.\n\nThe only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored late-August survey, shows Jackley ahead 47 to 43, closer than the district's typical margins. Prediction markets nonetheless price Gronli's chances at roughly 4 percent. The forecast expects Jackley to win by a solid double-digit margin, consistent with the state's partisan lean, though the thin polling leaves some room for a tighter result.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -15.31}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.035, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0242, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0357, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0239, "margin": -16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.019, "margin": -17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.015, "margin": -16.0}